# Cache rules for Cloudflare's static assets.
#
# style.css, app.js and the JSON files have no hash in their filenames, so a
# browser has no way to tell a new deploy from the copy it already has — it will
# happily serve the old one for days. That has bitten us twice: a page rendering
# completely unstyled long after the fix shipped, and a CSS fix appearing not to
# work at all.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "don't store". The file is still cached; the browser
# just has to ask "is this still current?" first, and gets a cheap 304 when it
# is. That is exactly what we want for files that change on every deploy.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Images are content-stable — a new logo gets a new deploy but is rare, and a
# week of staleness on a favicon hurts nobody.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
